@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.2033 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1291 x i8] }> <{ [1291 x i8] c"# `abi_ptx`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#38788]\0A\0A[#38788]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/38788\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AWhen emitting PTX code, all vanilla Rust functions (`fn`) get translated to\0A\22device\22 functions. These functions are *not* callable from the host via the\0ACUDA API so a crate with only device functions is not too useful!\0A\0AOTOH, \22global\22 functions *can* be called by the host; you can think of them\0Aas the real public API of your crate. To produce a global function use the\0A`\22ptx-kernel\22` ABI.\0A\0A<!-- NOTE(ignore) this example is specific to the nvptx targets -->\0A\0A``` rust,ignore\0A#![feature(abi_ptx)]\0A#![no_std]\0A\0Apub unsafe extern \22ptx-kernel\22 fn global_function() {\0A    device_function();\0A}\0A\0Apub fn device_function() {\0A    // ..\0A}\0A```\0A\0A``` text\0A$ xargo rustc --target nvptx64-nvidia-cuda --release -- --emit=asm\0A\0A$ cat $(find -name '*.s')\0A//\0A// Generated by LLVM NVPTX Back-End\0A//\0A\0A.version 3.2\0A.target sm_20\0A.address_size 64\0A\0A        // .globl       _ZN6kernel15global_function17h46111ebe6516b382E\0A\0A.visible .entry _ZN6kernel15global_function17h46111ebe6516b382E()\0A{\0A\0A\0A        ret;\0A}\0A\0A        // .globl       _ZN6kernel15device_function17hd6a0e4993bbf3f78E\0A.visible .func _ZN6kernel15device_function17hd6a0e4993bbf3f78E()\0A{\0A\0A\0A        ret;\0A}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
