@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3144 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [811 x i8] }> <{ [811 x i8] c"# `trait_alias`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#41517]\0A\0A[#41517]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/41517\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `trait_alias` feature adds support for trait aliases. These allow aliases\0Ato be created for one or more traits (currently just a single regular trait plus\0Aany number of auto-traits), and used wherever traits would normally be used as\0Aeither bounds or trait objects.\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(trait_alias)]\0A\0Atrait Foo = std::fmt::Debug + Send;\0Atrait Bar = Foo + Sync;\0A\0A// Use trait alias as bound on type parameter.\0Afn foo<T: Foo>(v: &T) {\0A    println!(\22{:?}\22, v);\0A}\0A\0Apub fn main() {\0A    foo(&1);\0A\0A    // Use trait alias for trait objects.\0A    let a: &Bar = &123;\0A    println!(\22{:?}\22, a);\0A    let b = Box::new(456) as Box<dyn Foo>;\0A    println!(\22{:?}\22, b);\0A}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
